// logos.std.wql.why — THE JUSTIFICATION AS A VALUE (ADR 0024 S4o).
//
// Three rounds of this axis shipped green and were then found to carry a false
// justification, and every time the class was the same: THE JUSTIFICATION DRIFTED
// FROM THE MECHANISM. A ground was a SENTENCE, composed at the moment of deciding
// by one of ten producers; the mechanism it described then moved and the sentence
// stayed. Measured at the round before this one, on the wql/deem corpus:
//
//   • 59 of 259 plans appended "the order axis was never entered" to a ground that,
//     one clause earlier IN THE SAME STRING, said an anti join / a traversal / the
//     absence of `order by` had refused them. The suffix was keyed on `nperm == 0`,
//     which is true both of a query with no join and of a chain the axis entered and
//     refused BEFORE the derivation ran. A count that means two things is not a fact
//     — the same defect the round before had just fixed one level up.
//
//   • `wql_join_order_multi_e2e::q5`'s trace said "24 permutations … 8 admissible,
//     1 carried as nests" while its plan said `considered()` 0 and "nothing was
//     considered". Both numbers were true of DIFFERENT things (nests emitted vs
//     candidates carried in a table) and nothing named the difference.
//
// Patching the strings again would buy one more round. So the ground stops being a
// string:
//
//   THE DECISION RECORDS A `Why` — WHICH ANTECEDENT FAILED, AND THE OPERANDS IT
//   FAILED ON. PROSE IS RENDERED FROM THAT RECORD, AT THE EDGE, BY ONE FUNCTION.
//
// A sentence cannot outlive the mechanism it describes if there is no sentence: the
// only text in this compiler that describes a join-order decision is produced by
// `why_render` from a record the decision itself filled, and both destinations —
// `plan_trace` and the plan's `explain()` — call it. They cannot disagree because
// there is one of them.
//
// ── THE THREE STATES A COUNT COULD NOT DISTINGUISH ───────────────────────────
// `why_axis` is the census's FIRST number and the one this module exists for:
//
//   AX_NONE      there is no order axis at all — this query has no join to reorder.
//   AX_REFUSED   the axis was ENTERED and refused BEFORE enumeration. `ground()`
//                names which antecedent failed; `enumerated()` is 0 for the same
//                reason it is 0 above, which is exactly why the count could never
//                have separated the two.
//   AX_SEARCHED  the derivation ran: `enumerated()` permutations walked,
//                `proved()` admissible, `considered()` carried as candidates.
//
// ⚠⚠ AND IT IS A FIELD, WRITTEN BY THE DECISION. This paragraph used to say the
// opposite — "derived from `ground`, not stored beside it; a state field set next to a
// code is a second place to be wrong" — and the reasoning was the defect. It is true
// that a derived state cannot contradict the ground; what it can contradict is the
// QUERY, and it did. `why_axis_of` partitioned the CODE SPACE (0–9 no axis, 10–19
// refused, 20+ searched), `WG_AGG` is 6, and nine corpus plans with an explicit join
// announced "this query has no join whose order a plan could choose" one trace line
// under their own `hash join on i64`. A range couples two independent decisions — what
// the ground is, and which state it was reached in — into one number, and the second
// moves silently when the first is extended.
//
// There is no function from ground to state to write, because the same ground occurs
// in two states: an aggregate over a bare scan has no order axis, an aggregate over a
// join has one and this ground is what refused it. `Why.axis` is the only answer,
// `why_set` is the only write of the verdict, and `why_of` takes the state as a
// PARAMETER — a default would be a band by another name (ADR 0024 S4p).
//
// ── WHAT THE PLAN PAYS FOR THIS ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// NOTHING IT DID NOT ASK FOR. The record is a COMPILE-TIME value: it lives in the
// metaprogram, it is rendered once where the plan's type is emitted, and what reaches
// the artifact is FIVE CONSTANT-RETURNING METHODS — `axis`, `ground`, `operand`,
// `refused`, and since S4q `explain` too. A plan struct gains no field and a `prepare`
// gains no store, the rule `has_tbl` and `proved()` already follow.
//
// ⚠ `explain()` USED TO BE A FIELD, AND THE ROUND THAT MADE IT ONE CLAIMED IT COST
// +8 BYTES. It did not: the claim measured total FILE size at -O2, where `.debug_str`
// had shrunk for unrelated reasons, while the suite compiles at -O0. The LOADED image
// (text+data+bss) grew +1168 bytes on `wql_deferred_plan_e2e`. And it could not have
// been free by construction — `prepare` STORED the text into the plan, so a live
// constructor referenced the literal and `--gc-sections` could never drop it.
// Measured after: a program that constructs five plans and never calls `explain()`
// links ZERO justification literals (was five) and is 2944 bytes smaller;
// `tests/logos/why_size_gate.sh` pins both halves. The text itself is unchanged —
// the justification is the deliverable, and what moved is only who pays for it.
//
// ── AND THE LIFETIME PROBLEM GOES AWAY WITH THE SENTENCES ────────────────────
// A composed ground used to be a `str` VIEW INTO A CALLER'S BUFFER, held from the
// decision until the artifact was written, because `push_str_lit` needs it alive at
// emission — one round shipped a use-after-free doing exactly that, and the buffer
// had to be hoisted two frames up and documented as untouchable. A record holds no
// composed text: every `str` in it is either a literal from a table in this file or
// a name the Writ/`MacroParams` owns for the whole compile. Composition happens at
// the edge, into the buffer that is about to be escaped, and lives one statement.
package logos.std.wql.why;

use logos.lang.str;
use logos.mem.string;
use logos.std.wql.join_cost;   // JC_MAX_FL / JC_MAX_CAND / jc_model_words — the bounds a remedy names

// ── THE CENSUS STATES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pub fn AX_NONE() -> i32     { return 0i32; }
pub fn AX_REFUSED() -> i32  { return 1i32; }
pub fn AX_SEARCHED() -> i32 { return 2i32; }

// ── THE GROUNDS: WHICH ANTECEDENT FAILED ─────────────────────────────────────
// A GROUND IS A CODE AND NOTHING ELSE. The numbers are still grouped and the gaps
// are still there, because a reader scanning the list wants like beside like — but
// NOTHING READS THE RANGE, and the grouping carries no meaning a program may act on.
//
// ⚠⚠ IT USED TO, AND THAT WAS THIS AXIS'S FOURTH JUSTIFICATION DEFECT, INSIDE ITS
// OWN CURE. `why_axis_of` mapped 0–9 to `AX_NONE`, 10–19 to `AX_REFUSED`, 20+ to
// `AX_SEARCHED`, and the census state was therefore a PREDICATE OVER A CODE RANGE.
// That couples two independent decisions into one number — WHAT the ground is, and
// WHICH STATE the query is in — and the second changes silently when the first is
// extended. Measured at `df129585`: `WG_AGG` (6) sits in the "no axis" band, so
// `wql_join_group_e2e::region_totals` — a query whose own trace line one row above
// reads `[plan] d -> hash join on i64` — announced "this query has no join whose
// order a plan could choose". Nine corpus plans, two of them carrying an `order by`
// as well; a `where 1 > 2` over a join reached the same sentence on `WG_FALSE_FILTER`.
//
// The same ground legitimately occurs in TWO states: an aggregate over a bare scan
// has no order axis, an aggregate over a join has one and refuses it. No assignment
// of `WG_AGG` to a band can be right for both, so the band is gone: `Why.axis` is a
// FIELD, written by the code that knows whether the query has a join (ADR 0024 S4p).
// Adding a ground now cannot move any plan's state.
//
// ⚠ `WG_UNSET` IS A DEFECT, NOT A GROUND. It is what an unfilled record holds, and
// every renderer names it as one rather than falling through to a neighbour's
// sentence — the default-DENY rule the rest of this axis already follows.
pub fn WG_UNSET() -> i32        { return 0i32; }
pub fn WG_SCAN() -> i32         { return 1i32; }
pub fn WG_HEAD() -> i32         { return 2i32; }
pub fn WG_IDENTITY() -> i32     { return 3i32; }
pub fn WG_FALSE_FILTER() -> i32 { return 4i32; }
pub fn WG_FALSE_PRED() -> i32   { return 5i32; }
pub fn WG_AGG() -> i32          { return 6i32; }

// 10 (`WG_NO_STEP`) and 16 (`WG_ONE_FLOAT`) are DELETED (2026-10-04), refuted
// rather than witnessed, and 19 (`WG_CROSS`) with them: `decide_join_orders`
// is called only with a chain that
// has a step, and `decide_over_set` only after the first step was found to be
// neither an anti join nor a traversal, so two sources always float; and every
// floatable step carries an `on` (the grammar requires one on a classic join,
// and the gpath and magic-set rewrites set one), so C5's bijection never lacks a
// predicate. All three sites are invariants now (`join_order.logos`).
pub fn WG_EDGE_FIRST() -> i32   { return 11i32; }
pub fn WG_ANTI_FIRST() -> i32   { return 12i32; }
pub fn WG_NO_SORT() -> i32      { return 13i32; }
pub fn WG_KEY_ORDER() -> i32    { return 14i32; }
pub fn WG_UNDECIDED() -> i32    { return 15i32; }
pub fn WG_MAX_FL() -> i32       { return 17i32; }

pub fn WG_MAX_CAND() -> i32     { return 20i32; }
pub fn WG_REFUSED() -> i32      { return 21i32; }
pub fn WG_ADMITTED() -> i32     { return 22i32; }
pub fn WG_DEFERRED() -> i32     { return 23i32; }
pub fn WG_OUTER() -> i32        { return 24i32; }   // the chain has an outer join

// ⚠ `why_axis_of(g)` USED TO LIVE HERE AND IS DELIBERATELY GONE. There is no
// function from a ground to a state, because there is no such function to write:
// `WG_AGG` is `AX_NONE` over a bare scan and `AX_REFUSED` over a join, and the same
// holds for `WG_FALSE_FILTER` and `WG_FALSE_PRED`. Anything reconstructing the state
// from the code would be reintroducing the coupling; `Why.axis` is the only answer.

// ── WHY POINT (1) COULD OR COULD NOT MEASURE A SIDE ──────────────────────────
// The per-side size classification, moved here from `join_order` with the rest of
// the vocabulary: the codes are OPERANDS of `WG_DEFERRED`, so they
// belong beside the record that carries them. `join_order::prep_size_reason` is
// still the one rule that ASSIGNS them — it needs the rel registry — and this file
// is the one place that says what each one MEANS and what repairs it.
pub fn SZ_OK() -> i32      { return 0i32; }
// 1 (`SZ_STREAMS`) is DELETED (2026-10-04) with `WG_NO_SIZE` (18): under `order by`,
// the only way into the size facts, every join source is materialized, so no
// streamed side is ever classified (`join_order::prep_size_reason`).
pub fn SZ_DERIVED() -> i32 { return 2i32; }
pub fn SZ_LOCAL() -> i32   { return 3i32; }

// ── THE REFUSAL GROUNDS OF THE DERIVATION ────────────────────────────────────
// A code per constraint, so the census the trace prints and the ground the plan
// records come from one table. `RJ_NONE` is admitted.
pub fn RJ_NONE() -> i32     { return 0i32; }
pub fn RJ_PINDEP() -> i32   { return 1i32; }
pub fn RJ_PREDBASE() -> i32 { return 2i32; }
pub fn RJ_PREDDUP() -> i32  { return 3i32; }
pub fn RJ_RESCAN() -> i32   { return 4i32; }
pub fn RJ_DEDUP() -> i32    { return 5i32; }
// 6 (`RJ_SHAPE`) and 7 (`RJ_PREDPIN`) are DELETED (2026-10-04): unreachable
// once a step's `on` is scoped (`join_order::derive_orders` holds them as
// panics). `RJ_N` stays 8: the census is spliced into generated code as eight
// literals (`rj_at`), and the two slots are always 0.
pub fn RJ_N() -> i64        { return 8i64; }

// ── THE RECORD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/// WHAT THE DECISION CONCLUDED AND WHAT IT CONCLUDED IT FROM — the minimal set of
/// facts entailing the verdict, in the form the decision itself held them.
///
/// ⚠ EVERY FIELD IS A VALUE THE DECISION USED, never a copy recomputed for display.
/// A second computation is a second place to drift, which is the disease and not the
/// cure: `sfirst` is the dedup the deferral itself performed, `ssz` is the very
/// expression the emitted `run` will read, `rjn` is the census the enumeration
/// counted. Nothing here is derivable-and-derived twice.
///
/// `ground`  WHICH ANTECEDENT FAILED (`WG_*`). The whole verdict in one number.
/// `axis`    THE CENSUS STATE (`AX_*`) — was there an order axis at all, was it
///           entered and refused before enumeration, did the derivation run. A
///           FIELD, written by the decision, and INDEPENDENT of `ground`: the same
///           ground occurs in two states (an aggregate over a scan has no axis; an
///           aggregate over a join has one and refuses it), so no function of the
///           code can supply it. ⚠ Every write of `ground` goes through `why_set`,
///           which writes both — a ground assigned on its own would leave a stale
///           state, which is the defect this field exists to end.
/// `nfl`     floatable sources — the operand of `WG_MAX_FL` and the width of the
///           per-side arrays below.
/// `nperm`   permutations ENUMERATED. 0 in both `AX_NONE` and `AX_REFUSED`, which
///           is why it is not the state.
/// `nadm`    permutations PROVED ADMISSIBLE — the operand of `WG_MAX_CAND`.
/// `ncand`   candidates CARRIED IN THE TABLE; this is `considered()` exactly, and it
///           is 0 whenever the plan carries no table.
/// `nnest`   loop nests EMITTED. ⚠ NOT THE SAME NUMBER AS `ncand`, and conflating
///           them is how the trace came to say "1 carried as nests" beside a plan
///           reporting `considered()` 0: a chain whose reorder was declined whole
///           still emits ONE nest — the query's own order — while carrying NO
///           candidate table. Both numbers are facts; neither is the other.
/// `rjn`     refusals per `RJ_*` code. The conclusion "no other order is admissible"
///           is entailed by the CONJUNCTION of these, so the record keeps all of
///           them and the renderer states all of them, in CODE order.
/// `key`     `WG_KEY_ORDER`'s operand: the `order by` key's LOGOS TYPE NAME, the
///           exact string `el_order_faithful` was asked about.
/// `keywhy`  the failed condition `el` answered with, carried rather than re-asked.
/// `nsd`     described sides — `nfl` on the deferred path, 0 elsewhere.
/// `scode`   per side, the `SZ_*` classification the deferral was DECIDED on.
/// `ssrc`    per side, the source text — the operand a remedy is addressed to.
/// `srep`    per side, how many positions that same source occupies. "This source
///           supplies three of the four numbers" is a fact about the query.
/// `sfirst`  is this side the FIRST position of its source? The dedup, performed
///           once, by the decision, so no consumer repeats it.
/// `ssz`     per side, the size EXPRESSION that will be read. For a deferred plan
///           the fact fields are all -1, so this text is the only account of WHAT
///           will be compared.
pub struct Why {
    pub ground: i32,
    pub axis:   i32,
    pub nfl:    i64,
    pub nperm:  i64,
    pub nadm:   i64,
    pub ncand:  i64,
    pub nnest:  i64,
    pub rjn:    [i64; 8],
    pub key:    str,
    pub keywhy: str,
    pub nsd:    i64,
    pub scode:  [i32; 4],
    pub ssrc:   [str; 4],
    pub srep:   [i64; 4],
    pub sfirst: [bool; 4],
    pub ssz:    [str; 4],
}

/// An UNSET record — `WG_UNSET`, which every renderer names as a defect. One nest is
/// the floor because a query that emitted none would have no body.
pub fn why_new() -> Why {
    return Why { ground: WG_UNSET(), axis: AX_NONE(), nfl: 0i64, nperm: 0i64, nadm: 0i64,
                 ncand: 0i64, nnest: 1i64, rjn: [0i64; 8],
                 key: "", keywhy: "", nsd: 0i64,
                 scode: [0i32; 4], ssrc: ["", "", "", ""], srep: [0i64; 4],
                 sfirst: [false; 4], ssz: ["", "", "", ""] };
}

/// THE ONE WRITE OF THE VERDICT — the ground AND the state it was reached in, set
/// together because they are two independent facts about one decision and a write of
/// either alone is a record that can contradict itself.
///
/// ⚠ THIS IS WHY IT IS A FUNCTION AND NOT TWO ASSIGNMENTS. `join_order` re-grounds a
/// record in flight (a derivation that ran, then declined; a deferral discovered
/// after the enumeration), and every one of those sites used to write `w.ground`
/// alone. With the state stored, `w.ground = g` on its own is exactly the drift the
/// field was introduced to prevent, so no site does it: they call this.
pub fn why_set(w: &mut Why, g: i32, ax: i32) {
    w.ground = g;
    w.axis = ax;
}

/// The record of a decision with ONE operand — the code — which is every ground
/// whose antecedent mentions nothing the query can vary.
///
/// ⚠ THE STATE IS A PARAMETER, NOT A DEFAULT. A default would be a band by another
/// name: the caller that knows the shape of the query is the only thing that knows
/// whether the axis existed, and making it say so is what stops the next ground
/// added to the table from inheriting a neighbour's census.
pub fn why_of(g: i32, ax: i32) -> Why {
    let mut w: Why = why_new();
    why_set(&mut w, g, ax);
    return w;
}

/// `WG_KEY_ORDER`: the operands are the key's TYPE NAME and the condition `el` says
/// its emitted comparison fails. Both are carried, not re-asked — the plan's
/// `operand()` answers the first, and a reader who disagrees with the verdict can
/// check it against the type they wrote.
pub fn why_key(tn: str, why: str, ax: i32) -> Why {
    let mut w: Why = why_of(WG_KEY_ORDER(), ax);
    w.key = tn;
    w.keywhy = why;
    return w;
}

pub fn why_axis(w: &Why) -> i32 { return w.axis; }

/// THE OPERAND A PROGRAM CAN READ — one `str`, because one is what a plan can carry
/// as a constant and because every ground has at most one operand that is not a
/// number. The key's type name where a key failed; the FIRST source that lost its
/// measurement where a size did; empty where the ground's operands are all counts
/// (which `enumerated`/`proved`/`considered`/`refused` already answer).
pub fn why_operand(w: &Why) -> str {
    if w.ground == WG_KEY_ORDER() { return w.key; }
    if w.ground == WG_DEFERRED() {
        let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
        while i < w.nsd {
            if w.scode[i] != SZ_OK() { return w.ssrc[i]; }
            i = i + 1i64;
        }
    }
    return "";
}

/// How many DISTINCT refusal grounds the census holds. `RJ_NONE` is admission and is
/// never counted.
pub fn why_rj_distinct(w: &Why) -> i64 {
    let mut n: i64 = 0i64;
    let mut k: i64 = 1i64;
    while k < RJ_N() {
        if w.rjn[k] > 0i64 { n = n + 1i64; }
        k = k + 1i64;
    }
    return n;
}

// ── THE VOCABULARY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/// The ground's own sentence, WITHOUT its operands — the renderer splices those in.
/// Every one of these was a literal at a decision site before this module; they are
/// literals here because the antecedent each of them names is a literal too, and
/// that is the rule: a `why` may be a constant only where what it asserts cannot
/// vary with the query.
pub fn wg_words(g: i32) -> str {
    if g == WG_SCAN() {
        return "one source, no join: the access path is decided where the query compiles, and on that axis a measurement does not change the answer — a narrowing is never meaningfully worse than a scan";
    }
    if g == WG_HEAD() {
        return "the answer is the head row of one source: one access, no order and no join, so there is nothing for a measurement to decide";
    }
    if g == WG_IDENTITY() {
        return "the answer IS the source, borrowed unchanged — there is no plan to decide";
    }
    if g == WG_FALSE_FILTER() {
        return "the filter is constantly false, so the plan IS the empty answer — no fact about the data can change it";
    }
    if g == WG_FALSE_PRED() {
        return "the predicate is constantly false, so the plan IS `None` — no fact about the data can change it";
    }
    if g == WG_AGG() {
        return "an aggregate's output order is its groups' FIRST-OCCURRENCE order, which no sort restores, so the plan holds the query's own nest and there is nothing for a measurement to choose between";
    }
    if g == WG_EDGE_FIRST() {
        return "a traversal step's source is a field path of an outer row, so it cannot be an outermost loop — there is nothing to bind its base to";
    }
    if g == WG_ANTI_FIRST() {
        return "an anti join is not symmetric: the rows of the base with no match are a different question from the rows of the step with no match";
    }
    if g == WG_OUTER() {
        return "the chain has an outer join: which side keeps its unmatched rows is fixed by the written order, so no other order answers the same question";
    }
    if g == WG_NO_SORT() {
        return "the row order of a join IS the nest's, and this query names no other one — without `order by` there is no sequence to restore, so driving the other side would return the same rows in a different order";
    }
    if g == WG_UNDECIDED() {
        return "no plan decided this step's strategy: it comes after a traversal, and the planner stops at the traversal because the row var it binds is typed only once the traversal is stamped (`plan_decide_chain`) — so there is no decision to offer a second order for";
    }
    if g == WG_MAX_FL() {
        return "more floatable sources than a plan holds facts for (four): the permutation search and the plan's size table are both bounded there, so this chain keeps the query's own order rather than searching a truncated space";
    }
    if g == WG_MAX_CAND() {
        return "more admissible orders than an artifact carries nests (four): the reorder is declined whole rather than searched over a set chosen by enumeration order, so the query's own order is emitted";
    }
    // ⚠ DEFAULT-DENY. `WG_KEY_ORDER`, `WG_REFUSED`, `WG_ADMITTED` and `WG_DEFERRED`
    // have operands and are composed by the renderer, so reaching this line with one
    // of them is a bug in `why_render` and not a missing sentence; anything else is a
    // code nobody has named. Neither gets to borrow a neighbour's ground.
    return "this decision recorded a ground code with no sentence in `why::wg_words` — a defect in this compiler's justification vocabulary, not a property of the query";
}

/// THE REPAIR THE FAILED ANTECEDENT ADMITS. Derived from the code that recorded the
/// refusal, so the advice cannot name a repair the refusal's own ground contradicts.
///
/// ⚠ EMPTY IS AN ANSWER AND SO IS "THERE IS NONE". The `AX_NONE` grounds return ""
/// because their own sentence already says there is nothing for a measurement to
/// decide — a remedy clause there would be advice to change the query into a
/// different query. Where a repair genuinely does not exist (an anti join's
/// asymmetry), the sentence SAYS so rather than being omitted: silence reads as an
/// oversight, and a reader then goes looking for the surface that was not named.
pub fn wg_remedy(g: i32) -> str {
    if g == WG_EDGE_FIRST() {
        return "a traversal cannot lead: the remedy is a query whose first step is a classic join, with the traversal deeper in the chain where its base is already bound";
    }
    if g == WG_OUTER() {
        return "there is no repair on this axis — an outer join's kept side is what the query asked for; joining the inner steps first, in a rel, leaves a chain the axis can reorder";
    }
    if g == WG_ANTI_FIRST() {
        return "there is no repair on this axis — an anti join's asymmetry is what the query ASKED for, and transposing it would answer a different question. Moving the anti join off the first step (a classic join first) leaves a pair the axis can reason about";
    }
    if g == WG_NO_SORT() {
        return "add an `order by`: a named sequence is what makes two nests the same answer, and without one there is no sequence for a second nest to restore";
    }
    if g == WG_KEY_ORDER() {
        return "";
    }
    if g == WG_UNDECIDED() {
        return "join the source before the traversal, where its key is typed at planning time: a step after a traversal has no strategy to reason from, and a strategy the planner never decided is not a fact a source can supply";
    }
    if g == WG_MAX_FL() {
        return "fewer floatable sources in one chain — the bound is `join_cost::JC_MAX_FL()`, and it is the width of the plan's fact table, not a search budget that could be raised on its own";
    }
    if g == WG_MAX_CAND() {
        return "a shorter chain, or one more pinned step — the bound is `join_cost::JC_MAX_CAND()`, the nests one artifact carries for one join body, so carrying more orders is a decision about the ARTIFACT (one order per object file) and not about this query";
    }
    if g == WG_REFUSED() {
        return "whichever of the refusals above your query can lose — every one of them had to hold for the query's own order to be the only one left, so removing any one leaves an order the derivation would admit; not the first one listed";
    }
    return "";
}

/// Why point (1) has no number for this side — the failed antecedent, in the
/// vocabulary of the thing that failed.
pub fn sz_no_prepare_words(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == SZ_DERIVED() {
        return "is a source whose rows this query materializes and which declares no `size`: the binding is a local of the generated fn, so before the query's own prelude has run there is no number to read and obtaining one would mean running the query a plan may not run";
    }
    if r == SZ_LOCAL() {
        return "is a `rel` BLOCK OF THIS QUERY: its rows are produced by the query's own fixpoint into a local of the generated fn, so before the prelude has run there is no number to read and obtaining one would mean running the query a plan may not run";
    }
    // Default-DENY, stated: a code nobody has named yet does not get to borrow one of
    // the grounds above.
    return "has no size at point (1) for a reason this module has not named — the classification reached a code with no ground, which is a defect in `join_order::prep_size_reason` and not a property of the query";
}

/// THE REPAIR A FAILED SIDE ADMITS — one per code, because the codes were split
/// precisely where the repair differs.
///
/// ⚠ "THERE IS NONE, AND HERE IS WHAT THE SOURCE WOULD HAVE TO BECOME" IS AN ANSWER.
/// What is not an answer is naming a declaration surface the reader's source does not
/// have; that is the defect this function exists to make impossible, since the same
/// code that decided the refusal decides the advice.
pub fn sz_remedy_words(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == SZ_DERIVED() {
        return "declaring a size is ACTIONABLE for it: it already declares its rows through an `impl` (`rel <name> = <fn>;`), and a `size <name> = <fn>;` line beside that one is read by the same natspec, lands as a reporter call in `prepare`, and moves the whole decision back to point (1)";
    }
    if r == SZ_LOCAL() {
        return "there is NOTHING TO DECLARE A SIZE ON: a `rel` block is part of this query, not a source it was given, and the registry carries no size field for one (`plan_walker::reg_native` is the only writer of `rel_size_fn` and it reads a natspec). The decision returns to point (1) only if the relation stops being the query's — materialized by the caller and passed in as a source that declares a `size`";
    }
    return "no repair is derivable, because the classification reached a code this module has not named — a defect in `join_order::prep_size_reason` and not a property of the query";
}

/// What the side IS, for the account of the read that `run` actually makes.
///
/// ⚠ DEFAULT-DENY HERE TOO. This used to fall through to `SZ_OK`'s sentence, so an
/// unnamed code would have been described as "an input the caller passed in" — the
/// one answer that makes the deferral look unnecessary.
pub fn sz_run_words(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == SZ_DERIVED() || r == SZ_LOCAL() {
        return "a relation the prelude materialized for the query's own reasons";
    }
    if r == SZ_OK() {
        return "an input the caller passed in, which `prepare` COULD have measured";
    }
    return "a side whose classification reached a code this module has not named — a defect in `join_order::prep_size_reason`";
}

/// The constraint a refused permutation failed. `nfl` selects the PAIR wording where
/// the chain is a pair: with two sources "C6" and "C7" name a general constraint
/// whose instance a reader can state much more directly, and the sentence a pair
/// query recorded before the axis generalized is the one it still records.
pub fn rj_words(r: i32, nfl: i64) -> str {
    if r == RJ_PINDEP() {
        return "C4: a pinned step (an anti join or a traversal) would stand before a row var its `on` or its field-path source reads — the dependency is not bound yet at that depth";
    }
    if r == RJ_PREDBASE() {
        return "C5: a join predicate would land on the OUTERMOST loop, which carries none — in this order it reads no row var bound after the base (only the base's row, or no row var at all), and nothing here turns it into a filter on the scan";
    }
    if r == RJ_PREDDUP() {
        return "C5: two join predicates land on the same position and a step carries one `on` — this order would need a conjunction, which nothing here builds";
    }
    if r == RJ_RESCAN() {
        if nfl == 2i64 {
            return "the reverse direction has no equi-key that can be indexed, so driving the other side would rescan a source the query order reads once";
        }
        return "C6: this order has no indexable equi-key for a source the query's order reads exactly once, so it would rescan what the plan may already have left as a consumed iterator";
    }
    if r == RJ_DEDUP() {
        if nfl == 2i64 {
            return "both sides are the same source, so the two sizes are equal by construction — no measurement at either decision point can prefer one order, and the transposed nest could never be the one chosen";
        }
        return "C7: this order's (size, role) sequence is the one an earlier candidate already has, so it costs the same for every possible data and no measurement could ever select it";
    }
    return "admitted";
}

/// THE k-TH REFUSAL COUNT. Eight positional arguments rather than an array, because
/// the caller is GENERATED CODE: a plan's `refused(code)` is one call to this
/// function with its own census spliced in as eight literals, which costs the plan no
/// field and no store and puts the selection rule in stdlib in one copy.
///
/// ⚠ IT IS THE SAME ARRANGEMENT `join_cost::jc_size_at` USES, and for the same
/// reason: an array constructed per call would be a stack write per call for a fact
/// that is constant, on a method a caller reaches only when they are already reading
/// a justification.
pub fn rj_at(k: i32, n0: i64, n1: i64, n2: i64, n3: i64,
             n4: i64, n5: i64, n6: i64, n7: i64) -> i64 {
    if k == 0i32 { return n0; }
    if k == 1i32 { return n1; }
    if k == 2i32 { return n2; }
    if k == 3i32 { return n3; }
    if k == 4i32 { return n4; }
    if k == 5i32 { return n5; }
    if k == 6i32 { return n6; }
    if k == 7i32 { return n7; }
    // Outside the code space: not "no refusals", which is a real answer for a code
    // that exists. -1 is this compiler's spelling of "this was never asked for".
    return -1i64;
}

/// WHAT A DEFERRED PLAN DOES NOT HOLD, in one copy, for every ground a deferred
/// decision records.
///
/// ⚠ IT IS ONE FUNCTION BECAUSE IT WENT WRONG AS TWO SENTENCES. S4j disclosed
/// `agrees` and `margin`; S4k then added `order_ix` and `cost_of` to the surface and
/// did not come back, so a caller was told exactly which members to distrust and the
/// list was short by the two that had just been added. A list that must be extended
/// whenever the surface grows has to live at ONE address.
///
/// ⚠ AND IT NAMES THE ANSWERS, NOT JUST THE MEMBERS. `join_cost::JC_NOFACT()` is what
/// `cost_of` and `margin` return here, and `wql_deferred_plan_e2e` asserts the
/// equality against that function — so the sentence and the artifact cannot drift
/// apart without a fixture going red.
pub fn defer_not_held() -> str {
    return "per-call means the PREPARED surface holds none of the answer: `order_ix` is -1 (no order is named — `run` names one, per call, from `order_pick` on the lengths it reads there), `swap` is false for want of an order rather than for want of a transposition, `cost_of` and `margin` return `join_cost::JC_NOFACT()` (-2, `the facts this answer needs are not on this plan` — distinct from -1, `there is no such candidate`), `agrees` is vacuously true because nothing here can go stale, and `settled()` is false, which is the one member whose whole job is to say so";
}

// ── THE ONE RENDERER ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Everything below composes text, and NOTHING ELSE IN THIS COMPILER DOES, for a
// join-order decision. `join_order::jo_report` renders a record onto `plan_trace`
// and `rexpr_walk::emit_prepared_fns` renders the SAME record into the plan's `why`
// literal, so the trace and `explain()` cannot say different things — which they did
// (`q5`: "24 enumerated, 8 admissible, 1 carried" on one channel, "nothing was
// considered" on the other).

/// One source, named, with the number of positions it occupies where that is more
/// than one. A self-join binds the same source at two or three positions and
/// repeating its ground once per position is noise a reader has to diff.
fn push_src(out: &mut String, w: &Why, k: i64) {
    out.push_str("`");
    out.push_str(w.ssrc[k]);
    out.push_str("`");
    if w.srep[k] > 1i64 {
        out.push_str(" (");
        out.push_i64(w.srep[k]);
        out.push_str(" positions)");
    }
}

/// THE SEARCH SUMMARY, in the exact shape the `order search` trace line has always
/// had. It is a function because the census clause of `explain()` quotes it too:
/// one text, so the two channels report one set of numbers.
///
/// ⚠ FOUR NUMBERS, NOT THREE. `nnest` is last and it is NOT `ncand`: a chain whose
/// reorder was declined whole carries 0 candidates and still emits 1 nest.
pub fn why_push_search(w: &Why, out: &mut String) {
    out.push_i64(w.nperm);
    out.push_str(" permutations of ");
    out.push_i64(w.nfl);
    out.push_str(" floatable sources enumerated, ");
    out.push_i64(w.nadm);
    out.push_str(" admissible, ");
    out.push_i64(w.nnest);
    out.push_str(" carried as nests");
}

/// THE REFUSAL CENSUS: every ground, with its count, in CODE order.
///
/// ⚠ CODE ORDER, NOT ENUMERATION ORDER, and not "the first". `all_ports` in
/// `wql_gpath_e2e` refuses 5 permutations — 2 by C5, 3 by C7 — and the plan used to
/// carry the C5 sentence alone because C5 happened to fire on the first challenger.
/// The conclusion "the query's own order is the only one left" is entailed by the
/// CONJUNCTION: remove either ground and an order survives.
fn push_rj_census(w: &Why, out: &mut String) {
    let mut n: i64 = 0i64;
    let mut k: i64 = 1i64;
    while k < RJ_N() {
        if w.rjn[k] > 0i64 {
            if n > 0i64 { out.push_str("; "); }
            out.push_i64(w.rjn[k]);
            out.push_str("x [");
            out.push_str(rj_words(k as i32, w.nfl));
            out.push_str("]");
            n = n + 1i64;
        }
        k = k + 1i64;
    }
}

/// THE GROUND — the antecedent that failed, with the operands it failed on spliced
/// in where it has any.
fn push_ground(w: &Why, out: &mut String) {
    if w.ground == WG_KEY_ORDER() {
        out.push_str("`order by` names a sequence, but C1's licence is that the EMITTED comparison REALIZES that sequence, not that a key exists — and being total is one of that licence's conditions rather than the whole of it. This key (`");
        out.push_str(w.key);
        out.push_str("`) fails it: ");
        out.push_str(w.keywhy);
        out.push_str(". The row-index tiebreak that makes every nest yield the same sequence rests on that comparison, so with this key the answer would stay a fact about WHICH NEST collected the tuples — this chain keeps the query's own order");
        return;
    }
    if w.ground == WG_REFUSED() {
        if why_rj_distinct(w) > 1i64 {
            out.push_str("no other order is admissible, and that conclusion rests on ALL of the refusals rather than on the first one: ");
            out.push_i64(w.nperm - w.nadm);
            out.push_str(" of ");
            out.push_i64(w.nperm);
            out.push_str(" permutations were refused, on ");
            out.push_i64(why_rj_distinct(w));
            out.push_str(" distinct grounds — ");
            push_rj_census(w, out);
            return;
        }
        // ONE distinct ground: it is recorded verbatim, because there is nothing to
        // choose between and the pair case's own sentences are reached exactly as
        // before.
        let mut k: i64 = 1i64;
        while k < RJ_N() {
            if w.rjn[k] > 0i64 { out.push_str(rj_words(k as i32, w.nfl)); return; }
            k = k + 1i64;
        }
        out.push_str("no other order is admissible, and the derivation recorded no ground for any refusal — a defect in `join_order::derive_orders`, not a property of the query");
        return;
    }
    if w.ground == WG_ADMITTED() {
        if w.ncand == 2i64 {
            out.push_str("either side may drive: the plan indexes the SMALLER side and walks the larger, decided once in `prepare` from the sizes the plan asked for — the sort's tuple tiebreak makes both nests yield the same sequence");
        } else {
            out.push_str("more than two orders are admissible: every one of them is emitted as its own nest and `join_cost` prices them all in `prepare` from the sizes the plan asked for — the sort's tuple tiebreak makes every nest yield the same sequence, and `cost_of(ix)` reports what each one would have cost");
        }
        return;
    }
    if w.ground == WG_DEFERRED() {
        push_defer_ground(w, out);
        return;
    }
    out.push_str(wg_words(w.ground));
}

/// The ground a DEFERRED admission records, COMPOSED FROM THE PER-SIDE CODES the
/// deferral was decided on.
///
/// ⚠ WHAT THE OLD CONSTANT GOT WRONG, precisely: it said both sizes were lengths of
/// relations this query materializes anyway, and "not on any fact `prepare` can
/// hold". For `via_rel(ls, rs)` one of the two is `(rs).len()` on a slice PARAMETER —
/// a fact `prepare` holds happily. A reader was told no number was obtainable when
/// one of two was.
fn push_defer_ground(w: &Why, out: &mut String) {
    if w.ncand == 2i64 {
        out.push_str("either side may drive");
    } else {
        out.push_str("one of ");
        out.push_i64(w.ncand);
        out.push_str(" orders drives");
    }
    out.push_str(", and not on a fact `prepare` can hold, because ");
    let mut nno: i64 = 0i64;
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < w.nsd {
        if w.scode[i] != SZ_OK() && w.sfirst[i] {
            if nno > 0i64 { out.push_str("; "); }
            push_src(out, w, i);
            out.push_str(" ");
            out.push_str(sz_no_prepare_words(w.scode[i]));
            nno = nno + 1i64;
        }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    // ⚠ AND IF NO SIDE FAILED, SAY SO RATHER THAN EMITTING A SENTENCE WITH A HOLE.
    // `WG_DEFERRED` is recorded only where at least one side was refused at point (1),
    // so this is unreachable — and an unreachable branch that would produce broken
    // prose is still a ground a reader could be shown.
    if nno == 0i64 {
        out.push_str("the deferral was taken with every side measurable at point (1), which contradicts the condition that sets it — this is a defect in `join_order::decide_over_set`, not a property of the query");
    }
    // The sides point (1) COULD have measured. Naming them is the whole correction:
    // their presence is why "no fact was obtainable" was false, and their movement to
    // point (2) has a ground of its own.
    let mut nok: i64 = 0i64;
    let mut j: i64 = 0i64;
    while j < w.nsd {
        if w.scode[j] == SZ_OK() && w.sfirst[j] {
            if nok > 0i64 { out.push_str(", "); }
            else { out.push_str(". `prepare` COULD have measured "); }
            push_src(out, w, j);
            nok = nok + 1i64;
        }
        j = j + 1i64;
    }
    if nok > 0i64 {
        if nok == 1i64 { out.push_str(" — that side is read in `run` all the same"); }
        else           { out.push_str(" — those sides are read in `run` all the same"); }
        out.push_str(", because a cost may not mix a fact from point (1) with one from point (2): every size in one comparison comes from the one point at which every one of them is free, and one unmeasurable side is enough to choose which point that is");
    }
    out.push_str(". So the order is decided inside `run` — once per call, above the nest, from lengths that are one field read where they stand. ");
    out.push_str(defer_not_held());
}

/// THE CENSUS CLAUSE — the three states, as the numbers that distinguish them and as
/// the sentence a person reads. THIS is what replaces the suffix keyed on
/// `nperm == 0` that asserted "the order axis was never entered" for 59 of 259 plans
/// whose own ground, one clause earlier, said which antecedent of the axis had
/// refused them: the clause is selected by `why_axis`, so a refusal cannot be
/// described as an absence.
///
/// ⚠ AND `why_axis` IS NOW A FIELD READ. It was a range test over the ground code for
/// one round, and that round put `WG_AGG` in the absence band: nine plans with an
/// explicit join were told they had none. The clause below is unchanged; what changed
/// is that the thing selecting it is a fact the decision recorded rather than a fact
/// re-derived from how the grounds happen to be numbered.
fn push_census(w: &Why, out: &mut String) {
    let ax: i32 = why_axis(w);
    if ax == AX_NONE() {
        out.push_str(" [ORDER AXIS NOT ENTERED (`axis()` 0): this query has no join whose order a plan could choose, so nothing was permuted — `enumerated()` 0, `proved()` 0, `considered()` 0, and the plan carries no candidate table for `cost_of` to price]");
        return;
    }
    if ax == AX_REFUSED() {
        out.push_str(" [ORDER AXIS ENTERED AND REFUSED BEFORE ENUMERATION (`axis()` 1, `ground()` ");
        out.push_i64(w.ground as i64);
        out.push_str("): the antecedent above failed, so the derivation never ran and `enumerated()` is 0 — the SAME 0 a query with no join reports, which is why this is `axis()` 1 and not a count. `proved()` 0, `considered()` 0, no candidate table]");
        return;
    }
    out.push_str(" [ORDER AXIS SEARCHED (`axis()` 2): ");
    why_push_search(w, out);
    out.push_str(" — `enumerated()` ");
    out.push_i64(w.nperm);
    out.push_str(", `proved()` ");
    out.push_i64(w.nadm);
    out.push_str(", `considered()` ");
    out.push_i64(w.ncand);
    if w.ncand == 0i64 {
        out.push_str(". NO CANDIDATE TABLE IS CARRIED, and NOT because nothing was proved — `proved()` and `considered()` differ here, which is exactly the reading a single count could not give");
    }
    out.push_str("]");
}

/// THE REMEDY CLAUSE, derived from the failed antecedent and its operands.
///
/// ⚠ ONE CLAUSE PER FAILING CLASS, NOT ONE PER QUERY, on the deferred path.
/// `db_i64_leaves` defers on two `rel` blocks and `iter_step` on a declared source; a
/// query that mixed the two would have had a single sentence covering both, which is
/// how one remedy came to be printed for sources that cannot take it. Class order is
/// CODE order, the same rule the refusal census follows.
fn push_remedy(w: &Why, out: &mut String) {
    if w.ground == WG_DEFERRED() {
        let mut nw: i64 = 0i64;
        let mut code: i64 = 1i64;
        while code < 4i64 {
            let mut n: i64 = 0i64;
            let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
            while i < w.nsd {
                if (w.scode[i] as i64) == code && w.sfirst[i] {
                    if n > 0i64 { out.push_str(", "); }
                    else if nw > 0i64 { out.push_str("; "); }
                    else { out.push_str(". THE REMEDY, derived from what each refused side IS: "); }
                    push_src(out, w, i);
                    n = n + 1i64;
                }
                i = i + 1i64;
            }
            if n > 0i64 {
                out.push_str(" — ");
                out.push_str(sz_remedy_words(code as i32));
                nw = nw + 1i64;
            }
            code = code + 1i64;
        }
        if nw > 0i64 { return; }
    }
    if w.ground == WG_KEY_ORDER() {
        // The repair is inside `el`'s own answer — it names the key types whose
        // emitted comparison realizes an order — and quoting it twice would be the
        // second copy this module exists to prevent.
        return;
    }
    let r: str = wg_remedy(w.ground);
    if r.len() == 0i64 { return; }
    out.push_str(". THE REMEDY, derived from the antecedent that failed: ");
    out.push_str(r);
}

/// THE ONE RENDERER. Ground, then census, then remedy — the DL-reasoner shape: the
/// facts and the rule that entail the conclusion, then which antecedent failed, then
/// what would have to change for it to hold.
///
/// ⚠ ITS OUTPUT IS ESCAPED INTO GENERATED SOURCE by `prepared::push_str_lit`, so the
/// caller's buffer must live until that call — one statement, in the frame that
/// escapes it. That is the whole of the lifetime discipline now: there is no composed
/// `str` on the record and nothing to keep alive across the decision.
pub fn why_render(w: &Why, out: &mut String) {
    push_ground(w, out);
    push_census(w, out);
    push_remedy(w, out);
    // ⚠ THE DEFERRED APPENDIX IS PART OF THE RENDER, not something a consumer adds.
    // The emitter used to append it to the plan's copy alone, so the plan and the
    // `[plan] … -> drive either side in \`run\`` line differed by exactly this clause:
    // measured, 66 of 81 join-order verdict lines said something other than the
    // `explain()` of the plan the same decision produced. A clause a caller may add
    // is a clause one caller will forget.
    if w.ground == WG_DEFERRED() {
        out.push_str(" [in `run`: ");
        why_push_sizes(w, out);
        out.push_str("]");
    }
}

/// The DEFERRED appendix: WHAT will be compared, and where each number comes from.
/// Kept out of `why_render` because it is the account of the read `run` makes rather
/// than the ground of the decision, and because `jo_report` prints it on its own
/// channel (`sizes deferred to run`) where a reader looks for it.
///
/// ⚠ THE ANNOTATIONS COME FROM THE RECORD, not from a second classification.
/// "each is the length of a binding the prelude already made" was false for a side
/// that is a PARAMETER — the prelude made nothing of it, and `prepare` could have
/// measured it.
pub fn why_push_sizes(w: &Why, out: &mut String) {
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < w.nsd {
        if i > 0i64 { out.push_str(" vs "); }
        out.push_str(w.ssz[i]);
        out.push_str(" [");
        out.push_str(sz_run_words(w.scode[i]));
        out.push_str("]");
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
}

// ══ THE JOIN STRATEGY'S GROUND — RULES AND FACTS, NOT SENTENCES (2026-10-02) ══
//
// The join-ORDER verdict above became a record in S4o; the per-step STRATEGY
// (hash / tree / loop) did not: `StepSel.why` was a sentence chosen by the branch
// that returned it, so nothing tied the words to the antecedents the branch had
// actually tested. Following the provenance design of Datalog engines (Soufflé's
// `explain`/`explainnegation`), the strategy is now a RULE over FACTS:
//
//   • an ANTECEDENT (`JA_*`) is one question the cascade asks about the step and its
//     key type — "is there an equi key", "does the key type implement Hash";
//   • a RULE (`JR_*`) is a conclusion with a BODY: the antecedents that must hold
//     (`jr_pos`) and those that must not (`jr_neg`). The cascade tries the rules in
//     order and records the first whose body holds;
//   • the GROUND (`JoinGround`) is the rule that fired plus the facts: which
//     antecedents were ASKED, which of those HELD. Two masks — the cascade's own
//     answers, never recomputed for display;
//   • `jg_failed(g, r)` is the negative explanation: for ANY rule, the asked
//     antecedents its body needed and did not get. "Why not a hash join" is
//     `jg_failed(g, JR_HASH())`, read off the same facts the decision used.
//
// The sentences are the renderer's (`jg_render`), and only the renderer's.
pub fn JA_EQUI_KEY() -> i32   { return 0i32; }  // the step has an equi-join key
pub fn JA_HASH() -> i32       { return 1i32; }  // K: Hash
pub fn JA_EQ() -> i32         { return 2i32; }  // K: Eq
pub fn JA_ORD() -> i32        { return 3i32; }  // K: Ord
pub fn JA_EQUALITY() -> i32   { return 4i32; }  // K has `==` at all (PartialEq or Eq; every lattice type)
pub fn JA_KEY_STORE() -> i32  { return 5i32; }  // the index can hold K (borrowed from the row, or Copy)
pub fn JA_SELF_IDENT() -> i32 { return 6i32; }  // K's own `==` is faithful (no NaN): EL_ID_OK
pub fn JA_SELF_ORD() -> i32   { return 7i32; }  // K's own `<` is faithful: EL_ORD_OK
pub fn JA_FORCE_TREE() -> i32 { return 8i32; }  // the tree tier is forced (a test knob)
pub fn JA_N() -> i32          { return 9i32; }

pub fn ja_bit(a: i32) -> i32 { return 1i32 << a; }

pub fn JR_UNSET() -> i32      { return 0i32; }
pub fn JR_LOOP_NOKEY() -> i32 { return 1i32; }  // no equi key: a nested loop is the only shape
pub fn JR_HASH() -> i32       { return 2i32; }
pub fn JR_TREE_FORCED() -> i32 { return 3i32; }
pub fn JR_TREE() -> i32       { return 4i32; }
pub fn JR_LOOP_EQ() -> i32    { return 5i32; }  // equality only: every pair is tested
pub fn JR_REFUSE() -> i32     { return 6i32; }  // no capability at all: the step is refused
pub fn JR_TRAVERSAL() -> i32  { return 7i32; }  // a traversal step: a loop by construction

/// The antecedents a rule's body needs TRUE.
pub fn jr_pos(r: i32) -> i32 {
    let k: i32 = ja_bit(JA_EQUI_KEY());
    let idx: i32 = ja_bit(JA_KEY_STORE());
    if r == JR_HASH() {
        return k | idx | ja_bit(JA_HASH()) | ja_bit(JA_EQ()) | ja_bit(JA_SELF_IDENT());
    }
    if r == JR_TREE_FORCED() || r == JR_TREE() {
        let t: i32 = k | idx | ja_bit(JA_ORD()) | ja_bit(JA_SELF_ORD());
        if r == JR_TREE_FORCED() { return t | ja_bit(JA_FORCE_TREE()); }
        return t;
    }
    if r == JR_LOOP_EQ() { return k | ja_bit(JA_EQUALITY()); }
    if r == JR_REFUSE()  { return k; }
    return 0i32;
}

/// The antecedents a rule's body needs FALSE.
pub fn jr_neg(r: i32) -> i32 {
    if r == JR_LOOP_NOKEY() { return ja_bit(JA_EQUI_KEY()); }
    if r == JR_HASH()       { return ja_bit(JA_FORCE_TREE()); }
    if r == JR_REFUSE()     { return ja_bit(JA_EQUALITY()); }
    return 0i32;
}

/// The facts and the rule they entailed. `asked`/`held` are masks over `JA_*`;
/// `key_tn` is the operand the key antecedents were asked of.
pub struct JoinGround { pub rule: i32, pub asked: i32, pub held: i32, pub key_tn: str }

pub fn jg_new(key_tn: str) -> JoinGround {
    return JoinGround { rule: JR_UNSET(), asked: 0i32, held: 0i32, key_tn: key_tn };
}

/// Record one answer. The cascade's only write of a fact.
pub fn jg_fact(g: &mut JoinGround, a: i32, v: bool) -> bool {
    g.asked = g.asked | ja_bit(a);
    if v { g.held = g.held | ja_bit(a); }
    return v;
}

/// Does rule `r`'s body hold on the facts? An antecedent not ASKED does not hold —
/// a rule cannot fire on a question nobody asked.
pub fn jr_holds(g: &JoinGround, r: i32) -> bool {
    let pos: i32 = jr_pos(r);
    let neg: i32 = jr_neg(r);
    if (pos & g.asked) != pos { return false; }
    if (pos & g.held) != pos { return false; }
    if (neg & g.held) != 0i32 { return false; }
    return true;
}

/// THE NEGATIVE EXPLANATION: the antecedents of rule `r` that were asked and came
/// out wrong for it (a needed one false, a forbidden one true), as a `JA_*` mask.
pub fn jg_failed(g: &JoinGround, r: i32) -> i32 {
    return (jr_pos(r) & g.asked & !g.held) | (jr_neg(r) & g.held);
}

pub fn ja_words(a: i32) -> str {
    if a == JA_EQUI_KEY()   { return "an equi-join key"; }
    if a == JA_HASH()       { return "Hash"; }
    if a == JA_EQ()         { return "Eq"; }
    if a == JA_ORD()        { return "Ord"; }
    if a == JA_EQUALITY()   { return "equality (`==`)"; }
    if a == JA_KEY_STORE()  { return "an index that can hold the key (borrowed from the row, or Copy)"; }
    if a == JA_SELF_IDENT() { return "a faithful `==` (no NaN)"; }
    if a == JA_SELF_ORD()   { return "a faithful `<`"; }
    if a == JA_FORCE_TREE() { return "the forced tree tier"; }
    return "an unnamed antecedent";
}

pub fn jr_name(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == JR_LOOP_NOKEY()  { return "loop_nokey"; }
    if r == JR_HASH()        { return "hash"; }
    if r == JR_TREE_FORCED() { return "tree_forced"; }
    if r == JR_TREE()        { return "tree"; }
    if r == JR_LOOP_EQ()     { return "loop_eq"; }
    if r == JR_REFUSE()      { return "refuse"; }
    if r == JR_TRAVERSAL()   { return "traversal"; }
    return "unset";
}

/// THE ONE RENDERER of a join-strategy ground — the sentence each rule has always
/// produced, now a function of the rule that fired rather than of the branch that
/// returned. `JR_UNSET` is named as the defect it is. It takes the RULE, not the
/// record: the sentence is a literal of the rule, so nothing of the record is
/// borrowed into it.
pub fn jg_render(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == JR_LOOP_NOKEY()  { return "no equi-join key — a nested loop is the only shape left"; }
    if r == JR_HASH()        { return "the key type is hashable — build once, probe per row"; }
    if r == JR_TREE_FORCED() { return "the tree tier is forced (LOGOS_JOIN_TREE) — the key is hashable but ordered access is being exercised"; }
    if r == JR_TREE()        { return "the key type is ordered but not hashable — a sorted index, not a hash one"; }
    if r == JR_LOOP_EQ()     { return "the key type has equality only — no index can be built, so every pair is tested"; }
    if r == JR_REFUSE()      { return "the key type has no usable capability"; }
    if r == JR_TRAVERSAL()   { return "a traversal step ranges over a field path of an outer row — the source is re-derived per bound row, so no index can be built over it"; }
    return "UNSET JOIN GROUND — a decision recorded no rule (a defect, not a reason)";
}

/// THE GROUND AS ONE WORD — what the plan carries (`core::CAtom.ground`,
/// `RJoin`/`RAnti.jground`) and the chain arrays copy, in place of the sentence
/// they used to carry: rule in bits 0-7, `asked` in 8-23, `held` in 24-39. One
/// `i64` in the slot the `str` held, so no node's key layout or capacity moves.
/// 0 is `JR_UNSET` with no facts — an undecided step, rendered as the defect it is.
pub fn jg_pack(g: &JoinGround) -> i64 {
    return (g.rule as i64) | ((g.asked as i64) << 8i64) | ((g.held as i64) << 24i64);
}
pub fn jg_rule_of(v: i64) -> i32 { return (v & 255i64) as i32; }
pub fn jg_unpack(v: i64, key_tn: str) -> JoinGround {
    return JoinGround { rule: jg_rule_of(v), asked: ((v >> 8i64) & 65535i64) as i32,
                        held: ((v >> 24i64) & 65535i64) as i32, key_tn: key_tn };
}
/// The sentence of a packed ground — `jg_render` of its rule.
pub fn jg_render_packed(v: i64) -> str { return jg_render(jg_rule_of(v)); }

/// The FACTS, machine-readable: `rule=<r> key=<K> held=[…] failed(hash)=[…]` —
/// what `LOGOS_TRACE_PLAN=facts` prints, so a fixture can assert the rule and the
/// failed antecedents instead of a substring of a sentence.
pub fn jg_push_facts(g: &JoinGround, out: &mut String) {
    out.push_str("rule="); out.push_str(jr_name(g.rule));
    out.push_str(" key="); out.push_str(g.key_tn);
    out.push_str(" held=[");
    push_ja_mask(out, g.held);
    out.push_str("] asked=[");
    push_ja_mask(out, g.asked);
    out.push_str("]");
    if g.rule != JR_HASH() && g.rule != JR_TRAVERSAL() && g.rule != JR_LOOP_NOKEY() {
        out.push_str(" not_hash=[");
        push_ja_mask(out, jg_failed(g, JR_HASH()));
        out.push_str("]");
    }
}

fn push_ja_mask(out: &mut String, m: i32) {
    let mut a: i32 = 0i32;
    let mut first: bool = true;
    while a < JA_N() {
        if (m & ja_bit(a)) != 0i32 {
            if !first { out.push_str(","); }
            out.push_str(ja_code(a));
            first = false;
        }
        a = a + 1i32;
    }
}

fn ja_code(a: i32) -> str {
    if a == JA_EQUI_KEY()   { return "equi_key"; }
    if a == JA_HASH()       { return "Hash"; }
    if a == JA_EQ()         { return "Eq"; }
    if a == JA_ORD()        { return "Ord"; }
    if a == JA_EQUALITY()   { return "eq_op"; }
    if a == JA_KEY_STORE()  { return "key_store"; }
    if a == JA_SELF_IDENT() { return "self_ident"; }
    if a == JA_SELF_ORD()   { return "self_ord"; }
    if a == JA_FORCE_TREE() { return "force_tree"; }
    return "?";
}

// ══ THE ACCESS PATH'S GROUND — the same shape, its own vocabulary (E2) ═══════
//
// How ONE rel is read against ONE filter (`plan_walker::plan_narrow_rel`). The
// decision was a cascade of `ap.scan(ri, "<sentence>")` returns plus one
// `ap.choose(…, <sentence>)`; each sentence named the first antecedent that
// failed, and nothing tied it to the test above it. Now each test records a fact,
// the rule that fires is the record, and `ag_render` is the only text — word for
// word the sentences the returns carried.
pub fn AA_WHERE() -> i32      { return 0i32; }   // the query has a filter
pub fn AA_OPS() -> i32        { return 1i32; }   // the source declares access operations
pub fn AA_COL() -> i32        { return 2i32; }   // a side of the filter is a column
pub fn AA_OWN_COL() -> i32    { return 3i32; }   // …of THIS source
pub fn AA_BOUND() -> i32      { return 4i32; }   // the other side is a literal or a name
pub fn AA_PARAM() -> i32      { return 5i32; }   // a name bound is a parameter of the fn
pub fn AA_PARAM_TY() -> i32   { return 6i32; }   // …of the column's type
pub fn AA_CMP() -> i32        { return 7i32; }   // the comparison is one a source answers
pub fn AA_COVER() -> i32      { return 8i32; }   // a declared operation covers it
pub fn AA_EXACT() -> i32      { return 9i32; }   // the chosen operation is exact for it
pub fn AA_MAY_DROP() -> i32   { return 10i32; }  // the filter belongs to this source alone
pub fn AA_N() -> i32          { return 11i32; }

pub fn AR_UNSET() -> i32           { return 0i32; }   // no filter reached this rel
pub fn AR_SCAN_ALL() -> i32        { return 1i32; }
pub fn AR_SCAN_NO_OPS() -> i32     { return 2i32; }
pub fn AR_SCAN_NO_COL() -> i32     { return 3i32; }
pub fn AR_SCAN_FOREIGN() -> i32    { return 4i32; }
pub fn AR_SCAN_NO_BOUND() -> i32   { return 5i32; }
pub fn AR_SCAN_NOT_PARAM() -> i32  { return 6i32; }
pub fn AR_SCAN_PARAM_TY() -> i32   { return 7i32; }
pub fn AR_SCAN_NO_CMP() -> i32     { return 8i32; }
pub fn AR_SCAN_NO_COVER() -> i32   { return 9i32; }
pub fn AR_EXACT_DROP() -> i32      { return 10i32; }
pub fn AR_EXACT_KEEP() -> i32      { return 11i32; }
pub fn AR_SUPERSET() -> i32        { return 12i32; }
pub fn AR_EXACT_CONJ() -> i32      { return 13i32; }   // exact for ONE conjunct of the filter (ADR 0026 F1)

/// The facts and the rule they entailed for one rel; packed with `jg_pack`'s
/// layout (`ag_pack`) to travel in the plan's per-rel arrays.
pub struct AccessGround { pub rule: i32, pub asked: i32, pub held: i32 }

pub fn ag_new() -> AccessGround { return AccessGround { rule: AR_UNSET(), asked: 0i32, held: 0i32 }; }

/// Record one answer — the cascade's only write of a fact.
pub fn ag_fact(g: &mut AccessGround, a: i32, v: bool) -> bool {
    g.asked = g.asked | ja_bit(a);
    if v { g.held = g.held | ja_bit(a); }
    return v;
}

pub fn ag_pack(g: &AccessGround) -> i64 {
    return (g.rule as i64) | ((g.asked as i64) << 8i64) | ((g.held as i64) << 24i64);
}
pub fn ag_unpack(v: i64) -> AccessGround {
    return AccessGround { rule: (v & 255i64) as i32, asked: ((v >> 8i64) & 65535i64) as i32,
                          held: ((v >> 24i64) & 65535i64) as i32 };
}

/// THE ONE RENDERER of an access-path ground.
pub fn ag_render(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == AR_SCAN_ALL()       { return "the query asks for every row — no filter to narrow to"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_OPS()    { return "the source declares no access operations"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_COL()    { return "neither side of the filter is a column"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_FOREIGN()   { return "the filter names a column this source does not have"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_BOUND()  { return "the comparison carries no bound a source could be given"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NOT_PARAM() { return "the bound is not a query parameter this fn takes"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_PARAM_TY()  { return "the parameter's type is not the column's, so it cannot be passed as the bound"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_CMP()    { return "the filter is not a comparison a source can answer"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_COVER()  { return "the source declares no operation covering that comparison on that column"; }
    if r == AR_EXACT_DROP()     { return "an operation EXACT for that comparison — the residual filter is redundant and was dropped"; }
    if r == AR_EXACT_KEEP()     { return "an operation exact for that comparison, but the filter ranges over more than this source, so it stays"; }
    if r == AR_SUPERSET()       { return "a covering operation; its rows are a superset, so the filter stays"; }
    if r == AR_EXACT_CONJ()     { return "an operation exact for ONE conjunct of the filter — the narrowest one; the other conjuncts still test each row, so the filter stays"; }
    return "no filter reaches this rel";
}

pub fn ar_name(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == AR_SCAN_ALL()       { return "scan_all"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_OPS()    { return "scan_no_ops"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_COL()    { return "scan_no_col"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_FOREIGN()   { return "scan_foreign_col"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_BOUND()  { return "scan_no_bound"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NOT_PARAM() { return "scan_not_param"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_PARAM_TY()  { return "scan_param_ty"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_CMP()    { return "scan_no_cmp"; }
    if r == AR_SCAN_NO_COVER()  { return "scan_no_cover"; }
    if r == AR_EXACT_DROP()     { return "exact_drop"; }
    if r == AR_EXACT_KEEP()     { return "exact_keep"; }
    if r == AR_SUPERSET()       { return "superset"; }
    if r == AR_EXACT_CONJ()     { return "exact_conj"; }
    return "unset";
}

fn aa_code(a: i32) -> str {
    if a == AA_WHERE()    { return "where"; }
    if a == AA_OPS()      { return "ops"; }
    if a == AA_COL()      { return "col"; }
    if a == AA_OWN_COL()  { return "own_col"; }
    if a == AA_BOUND()    { return "bound"; }
    if a == AA_PARAM()    { return "param"; }
    if a == AA_PARAM_TY() { return "param_ty"; }
    if a == AA_CMP()      { return "cmp"; }
    if a == AA_COVER()    { return "cover"; }
    if a == AA_EXACT()    { return "exact"; }
    if a == AA_MAY_DROP() { return "may_drop"; }
    return "?";
}

fn push_aa_mask(out: &mut String, m: i32) {
    let mut a: i32 = 0i32;
    let mut first: bool = true;
    while a < AA_N() {
        if (m & ja_bit(a)) != 0i32 {
            if !first { out.push_str(","); }
            out.push_str(aa_code(a));
            first = false;
        }
        a = a + 1i32;
    }
}

/// The facts, machine-readable: `rule=<r> held=[…] failed=[…]`, where `failed`
/// is the asked antecedents that did not hold — for a cascade, the one that ended
/// it (and, for a narrowing, the exactness/ownership that did not).
pub fn ag_push_facts(g: &AccessGround, out: &mut String) {
    out.push_str("rule="); out.push_str(ar_name(g.rule));
    out.push_str(" held=["); push_aa_mask(out, g.held);
    out.push_str("] failed=["); push_aa_mask(out, g.asked & !g.held);
    out.push_str("]");
}

// ══ HOW A REL TRAVELS, AND HOW MANY ROWS IT HAS — the mode and size grounds (E3) ══
//
// `access_plan_decide_mode` (stream vs materialize) and `access_plan_ask_size`
// wrote a sentence per rel; `plan_mark_rel_landings` later OVERWROTE the mode
// sentence for recursive and rel-block rels. Now each records facts on one
// `AccessGround` per rel and names a rule; a later pass ADDS its fact to the same
// record rather than replacing the text. The drained case renders the drain
// node's own sentence (the per-rel line and the node line quote one string, the
// rule `access_plan_decide_mode` already had).
pub fn MA_ITER() -> i32    { return 0i32; }   // the producer is an iterator
pub fn MA_ORDERED() -> i32 { return 1i32; }   // `order by` is over the column rows arrive sorted by
pub fn MA_DESC() -> i32    { return 2i32; }   // …descending
pub fn MA_DRAIN() -> i32   { return 3i32; }   // a drain node was inserted over it
pub fn MA_REC() -> i32     { return 4i32; }   // the rel is a member of a recursive SCC
pub fn MA_NATIVE() -> i32  { return 5i32; }   // the rel is a native (declared) source
pub fn MA_N() -> i32       { return 6i32; }

pub fn MR_UNSET() -> i32      { return 0i32; }
pub fn MR_CONTAINER() -> i32  { return 1i32; }
pub fn MR_ORDERED_REV() -> i32 { return 2i32; }
pub fn MR_ORDERED() -> i32    { return 3i32; }
pub fn MR_DRAINED() -> i32    { return 4i32; }
pub fn MR_STREAM() -> i32     { return 5i32; }
pub fn MR_FIXPOINT() -> i32   { return 6i32; }
pub fn MR_REL_HELPER() -> i32 { return 7i32; }

pub fn ZA_SIZE() -> i32       { return 0i32; }  // the source declares a size operation
pub fn ZR_UNSET() -> i32      { return 0i32; }
pub fn ZR_MEASURED() -> i32   { return 1i32; }
pub fn ZR_UNMEASURED() -> i32 { return 2i32; }

/// THE ONE RENDERER of a mode ground. `MR_DRAINED` has no sentence of its own:
/// the caller renders the drain node's (`node_why`), which is the point of it.
pub fn mr_render(r: i32, node_why: str) -> str {
    if r == MR_CONTAINER()   { return "materialized: the producer returns a container, not an iterator"; }
    if r == MR_ORDERED_REV() { return "streamed BACKWARD: the producer is an iterator over the column the rows already arrive sorted by, the plan reads it once, and `desc` is one landing at the end plus a backward pull"; }
    if r == MR_ORDERED()     { return "streamed: the producer is an iterator, the plan reads it once, and the `order by` is over the column the rows already arrive sorted by"; }
    if r == MR_DRAINED()     { return node_why; }
    if r == MR_STREAM()      { return "streamed: the producer is an iterator and the plan reads it once"; }
    if r == MR_FIXPOINT()    { return "materialized: this rel is recursive, so the semi-naive fixpoint accumulates its rows into a Vec the SCC driver grows — the plan builds this container rather than being handed one"; }
    if r == MR_REL_HELPER()  { return "materialized: the rel block's helper fn folds the body into a Vec and returns it, and the prelude binds the result — the container is built by code this compilation emitted, not handed over by a source"; }
    return "";
}
pub fn mr_name(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == MR_CONTAINER()   { return "container"; }
    if r == MR_ORDERED_REV() { return "ordered_rev"; }
    if r == MR_ORDERED()     { return "ordered"; }
    if r == MR_DRAINED()     { return "drained"; }
    if r == MR_STREAM()      { return "stream"; }
    if r == MR_FIXPOINT()    { return "fixpoint"; }
    if r == MR_REL_HELPER()  { return "rel_helper"; }
    return "unset";
}
pub fn zr_render(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == ZR_MEASURED()   { return "measured: the source reports its size, read once before the first row"; }
    if r == ZR_UNMEASURED() { return "unmeasured: the source declares no size operation, so the cardinality ORDINAL is all this plan has"; }
    return "";
}
fn ma_code(a: i32) -> str {
    if a == MA_ITER()    { return "iter"; }
    if a == MA_ORDERED() { return "ordered"; }
    if a == MA_DESC()    { return "desc"; }
    if a == MA_DRAIN()   { return "drain"; }
    if a == MA_REC()     { return "recursive"; }
    if a == MA_NATIVE()  { return "native"; }
    return "?";
}
fn push_ma_mask(out: &mut String, m: i32) {
    let mut a: i32 = 0i32;
    let mut first: bool = true;
    while a < MA_N() {
        if (m & ja_bit(a)) != 0i32 {
            if !first { out.push_str(","); }
            out.push_str(ma_code(a));
            first = false;
        }
        a = a + 1i32;
    }
}
pub fn mg_push_facts(g: &AccessGround, out: &mut String) {
    out.push_str("rule="); out.push_str(mr_name(g.rule));
    out.push_str(" held=["); push_ma_mask(out, g.held);
    out.push_str("] failed=["); push_ma_mask(out, g.asked & !g.held);
    out.push_str("]");
}

// ══ MAY THIS QUERY HAVE AN INCREMENTAL HANDLE — its ground (E3) ══════════════
//
// `rexpr_walk::incr_eligible` is a CASCADE: each test ends the decision when it
// fails, so its ground is the FIRST FAILED ANTECEDENT — the shape of S4o's `WG_*`,
// a code that names it, not a mask. Each code renders the sentence the cascade's
// `incr_decline(qn, "…")` used to carry, byte for byte; the three `EMIT_*` codes
// are the admitted shapes. `IR_REL_NOT_INCR`'s sentence is an operand (the rel
// registry's own ground), so it has no rendering here.
pub fn IR_JOIN_SRC_REL() -> i32 { return 1i32; }
pub fn IR_BASE_REL_JOINS() -> i32 { return 2i32; }
pub fn IR_REL_SLICE_COUNT() -> i32 { return 3i32; }
pub fn IR_REL_ROW_TY() -> i32 { return 4i32; }
pub fn IR_REL_COL_TY() -> i32 { return 5i32; }
pub fn IR_CHAIN_LONG() -> i32 { return 6i32; }
pub fn IR_JOIN_INSERT_ONLY() -> i32 { return 7i32; }
pub fn IR_JOIN_ANTI() -> i32 { return 8i32; }
pub fn IR_JOIN_EDGE() -> i32 { return 9i32; }
pub fn IR_JOIN_BYVAL() -> i32 { return 10i32; }
pub fn IR_JOIN_STREAMS() -> i32 { return 11i32; }
pub fn IR_SELF_JOIN() -> i32 { return 12i32; }
pub fn IR_JOIN_ROW_TY() -> i32 { return 13i32; }
pub fn IR_PRE_WHERE() -> i32 { return 14i32; }
pub fn IR_MODIFIERS() -> i32 { return 15i32; }
pub fn IR_GENERIC() -> i32 { return 16i32; }
pub fn IR_UDA() -> i32 { return 17i32; }
pub fn IR_AGG_STR() -> i32 { return 18i32; }
pub fn IR_KEY_STR() -> i32 { return 19i32; }
pub fn IR_RESULT_STR() -> i32 { return 20i32; }
pub fn IR_SELECT_NAME() -> i32 { return 21i32; }
pub fn IR_HAVING_NAME() -> i32 { return 22i32; }
pub fn IR_PROJ_STR() -> i32 { return 23i32; }
pub fn IR_REL_NOT_INCR() -> i32 { return 24i32; }
pub fn IR_EMIT_JOIN() -> i32 { return 25i32; }
pub fn IR_EMIT_REL() -> i32 { return 26i32; }
pub fn IR_EMIT_SCAN() -> i32 { return 27i32; }

pub fn ir_render(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == IR_JOIN_SRC_REL() { return "a JOIN-POSITION source is a DECLARED `rel` — the handle's joined side is stored as a weighted Z-set (`__s<k>`/`__s<k>w`) and a derived rel has no multiplicity to store: its rows come out of a set-semantics fixpoint over the ACCUMULATED input, which is state the join arm does not own"; }
    if r == IR_BASE_REL_JOINS() { return "the BASE source is a declared `rel` and the query also JOINS — one epoch would have to extend a set-semantics fixpoint total and integrate a weighted Z-set side, and the source TAG that tells them apart lives on `<q>_apply`, which a rel-backed query does not emit"; }
    if r == IR_REL_SLICE_COUNT() { return "a rel-backed query must have EXACTLY ONE slice parameter — `<q>_epoch` keeps the parameter list verbatim, so with two the caller passes both on every call and nothing says which is the delta; the join arm answers that with a source TAG on `<q>_apply`, which a rel-backed query does not emit"; }
    if r == IR_REL_ROW_TY() { return "the rel's INPUT ROW TYPE is not OWNABLE AND IDENTIFIABLE field by field — the handle accumulates every fact ever applied, so a `str` field is a borrow of source bytes it does not own and an `f64` field has no `==` that is identity (NaN != NaN, -0.0 == +0.0) for the insert presence gate to search on"; }
    if r == IR_REL_COL_TY() { return "a rel COLUMN is `str` or `f64` — the handle owns the fixpoint TOTAL, and a `str` column is a borrow while an `f64` column has no `==` that is identity for the shadow set that makes the fixpoint terminate"; }
    if r == IR_CHAIN_LONG() { return "the input is a JOIN CHAIN OF TWO OR MORE STEPS — rooting the nest at a step other than the base re-splits every equi-term's build/probe halves and re-places every floating predicate, which is `decide_join_orders`' derivation and this emitter does not run it"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_INSERT_ONLY() { return "the query JOINS and keeps the INSERT-ONLY surface (an aggregate accumulates in `f64` — decision D4), and the source TAG a join delta must carry lives on `<q>_apply`, which only the retracting surface emits"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_ANTI() { return "the join step is ANTI — anti is a MATCHCOUNT whose 0↔positive crossing must emit a retraction of a row that never changed, which is a second state machine and not the product rule"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_EDGE() { return "the join step is a TRAVERSAL (`edge`) — its source is re-derived per bound row, so there is no standalone relation for the handle to own or for a source tag to name"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_BYVAL() { return "the join step binds its row BY VALUE — the handle's stored side is a `Vec` this emitter binds by reference, and the two spellings are not interchangeable in the emitted predicate"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_STREAMS() { return "a join source STREAMS — an iterator yields its rows once, so the handle would have to be its only reader and the caller could never re-present it as a delta"; }
    if r == IR_SELF_JOIN() { return "the join is a SELF-JOIN — one relation in two chain positions, so one source tag would feed both, and folding a delta against a state that must already contain it is the double count this rule exists to avoid"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_ROW_TY() { return "a join source's ROW TYPE is not OWNABLE AND IDENTIFIABLE field by field — the handle stores whole rows of both sides, so a `str` field is a borrow of source bytes it does not own, a struct field is an ownership question this clause does not walk, and an `f64` field has no `==` that is identity (NaN != NaN, -0.0 == +0.0) for the Z-set's normal form to search on"; }
    if r == IR_PRE_WHERE() { return "a PRE-GROUP `where` filters rows before the fold, and that arm has never been folded incrementally — `having`, which sits above the group, IS admitted"; }
    if r == IR_MODIFIERS() { return "`order by` / `limit` / `distinct` act on the SNAPSHOT rather than on the fold — cheap to add, excluded here so the emitted surface stays what a fixture asserts"; }
    if r == IR_GENERIC() { return "the query is GENERIC — the handle type would have to carry the same type parameters and so would all three derived fns"; }
    if r == IR_UDA() { return "a USER AGGREGATE threads its own accumulator type through `_step`, which is outside `agg_acc_ty`'s domain"; }
    if r == IR_AGG_STR() { return "an aggregate COLUMN is `str`/`String` — a handle owns its cells and a `str` cell is a borrow of a source row it does not keep"; }
    if r == IR_KEY_STR() { return "the GROUP KEY is `str`/`String` — the dynamic engine solves this by interning into its own Writ, which is the one thing a typed handle exists not to need"; }
    if r == IR_RESULT_STR() { return "the RESULT element type is `str`/`String`"; }
    if r == IR_SELECT_NAME() { return "`select` reaches a name that is neither `key` nor an aggregate output — a source row (its index means nothing across epochs) or a scalar parameter (`<q>_snapshot` takes none)"; }
    if r == IR_HAVING_NAME() { return "`having` reaches a name that is neither `key` nor an aggregate output"; }
    if r == IR_PROJ_STR() { return "a projected COMPONENT is a `str`/`String` value, which the handle cannot hand back without borrowing something it does not own"; }
    if r == IR_EMIT_JOIN() { return "one join step over two owned relations, group by, weighted aggregates over self-contained types"; }
    if r == IR_EMIT_REL() { return "one bare scan over a RECURSIVE `rel`, group by, insert-only aggregates — the handle owns the accumulated input and the fixpoint TOTAL, and each epoch EXTENDS that total through the cross-epoch semi-naive driver"; }
    if r == IR_EMIT_SCAN() { return "one bare scan, group by, insert-only aggregates over self-contained types"; }
    return "";
}

pub fn ir_name(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == IR_JOIN_SRC_REL() { return "join_src_rel"; }
    if r == IR_BASE_REL_JOINS() { return "base_rel_joins"; }
    if r == IR_REL_SLICE_COUNT() { return "rel_slice_count"; }
    if r == IR_REL_ROW_TY() { return "rel_row_ty"; }
    if r == IR_REL_COL_TY() { return "rel_col_ty"; }
    if r == IR_CHAIN_LONG() { return "chain_long"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_INSERT_ONLY() { return "join_insert_only"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_ANTI() { return "join_anti"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_EDGE() { return "join_edge"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_BYVAL() { return "join_byval"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_STREAMS() { return "join_streams"; }
    if r == IR_SELF_JOIN() { return "self_join"; }
    if r == IR_JOIN_ROW_TY() { return "join_row_ty"; }
    if r == IR_PRE_WHERE() { return "pre_where"; }
    if r == IR_MODIFIERS() { return "modifiers"; }
    if r == IR_GENERIC() { return "generic"; }
    if r == IR_UDA() { return "uda"; }
    if r == IR_AGG_STR() { return "agg_str"; }
    if r == IR_KEY_STR() { return "key_str"; }
    if r == IR_RESULT_STR() { return "result_str"; }
    if r == IR_SELECT_NAME() { return "select_name"; }
    if r == IR_HAVING_NAME() { return "having_name"; }
    if r == IR_PROJ_STR() { return "proj_str"; }
    if r == IR_REL_NOT_INCR() { return "rel_not_incr"; }
    if r == IR_EMIT_JOIN() { return "emit_join"; }
    if r == IR_EMIT_REL() { return "emit_rel"; }
    if r == IR_EMIT_SCAN() { return "emit_scan"; }
    return "unset";
}

// ══ MAY THE HANDLE RUN BACKWARDS — the retraction ground (E3) ════════════════
// `rexpr_walk::incr_retract_eligible`: the first failed antecedent, as above.
pub fn RT_REC_REL() -> i32   { return 1i32; }   // backed by a recursive `rel` (DRed is the mechanism)
pub fn RT_FLOAT_ACC() -> i32 { return 2i32; }   // an aggregate accumulates in f64
pub fn RT_EXACT() -> i32     { return 3i32; }   // admitted: every aggregate inverts exactly

pub fn rt_render(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == RT_REC_REL()   { return "the query is backed by a RECURSIVE `rel` — a derived fact may support ITSELF through a cycle, so there is no amount to subtract; the correct mechanism is DRed (over-delete, compact, re-derive), a provenance state machine and not an inverse fold. \u26a0 AND DRed IS A PESSIMIZATION TODAY: measured 1.15-1.9x a from-scratch recompute, losing WORSE as the re-derived set grows, with no crossover anywhere in the reachable range \u2014 so admitting this shape is not a free capability, and the price must be named to the caller at the moment it becomes reachable. The repair that changes the direction is the EDB-delta occurrence list, which changes the ENUMERATION rather than choosing between two enumerations"; }
    if r == RT_FLOAT_ACC() { return "an aggregate accumulates in `f64` (a float `sum`, or ANY `avg` — it divides at snapshot out of a float running total), and `(S+x)-x != S` is an OPEN decision rather than an emitter's to take"; }
    if r == RT_EXACT()     { return "every aggregate in the list runs backwards exactly — `count` and integer `sum` invert exactly under their own checked predicate, `min`/`max` rescan a typed value→multiplicity map"; }
    return "";
}
pub fn rt_name(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == RT_REC_REL()   { return "rec_rel"; }
    if r == RT_FLOAT_ACC() { return "float_acc"; }
    if r == RT_EXACT()     { return "exact"; }
    return "unset";
}

// ══ WHAT A RETRACTION IS MATCHED ON — the bare scan's identity (2026-10-03) ══
// `rexpr_walk::emit_incremental`, the `sens` store: a retracted row must be one
// the handle holds, and "holds" is decided on one of two identities.
pub fn RI_ROW() -> i32       { return 1i32; }   // every field of the row
pub fn RI_FOOTPRINT() -> i32 { return 2i32; }   // the group key and the aggregate arguments

pub fn ri_render(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == RI_ROW()       { return "the WHOLE ROW, field by field — a `str` field is held as an owned `String`, a float field by `f64_canon_bits` (all zeros one value, all NaNs one value, the multiplicity map's identity), a field of a named type by its own `Eq` (copied, or cloned when it is not `Copy`) — so a retraction of a row the handle never held is refused even where it agrees on every value the fold reads, and a `count` sees the row and not only its group"; }
    if r == RI_FOOTPRINT() { return "the fold's FOOTPRINT, the group key followed by every aggregate argument — a field of the row is not a scalar, `str`, `String`, float, or a named type with `Eq` and `Copy` or `Clone` (or the row has more than 12 fields), so the row has no identity this store can hold; two rows that agree on the footprint are one row to this handle, and a `count` sees only the group"; }
    return "";
}
pub fn ri_name(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == RI_ROW()       { return "row"; }
    if r == RI_FOOTPRINT() { return "footprint"; }
    return "unset";
}

// ══ THE DRed EPOCH DRIVER — emitted or not, and why (E3) ═════════════════════
pub fn DR_EMIT() -> i32   { return 1i32; }   // the four-phase driver is emitted
pub fn DR_FLOAT() -> i32  { return 2i32; }   // an aggregate accumulates in f64
pub fn DR_MINMAX() -> i32 { return 3i32; }   // a min/max needs the retraction surface's map
pub fn dr_render(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == DR_EMIT()   { return "the four-phase DRed epoch driver `__wql_<q>_scc<c>_dred` — `_od` then `_odp` then `_cpt` then `_i`, on driver-local state, with `DE ⊆ __edb` enforced EXACTLY against the accumulated input before phase 1a and a SIGNED group fold (`__rm_<m>` at −1, the post-`_cpt` suffix at +1). ATOMIC AT THE HANDLE: every phase runs on a full local copy and the caller's handle is written once, at the end, so an `Err` from any phase or either fold half leaves it byte-identical. THE PUBLIC RETRACTION SURFACE FOLLOWS — `<q>_retract(&mut h, de, …)`, `<q>_epoch`'s signature exactly, forwarding here; `incr_retract_eligible` still declines (`retr` stays false, so no `<q>_apply` and no `__wd`) and the surface is emitted from this admission instead. ⚠ AND IT IS A PESSIMIZATION THE CALLER PAYS FOR: measured 1.15-1.9x a from-scratch recompute over the survivors, losing WORSE as the re-derived set grows, with no crossover anywhere in the reachable range — the repair that changes the direction is the EDB-delta occurrence list, which changes the ENUMERATION rather than choosing between two enumerations"; }
    if r == DR_FLOAT()  { return "an aggregate accumulates in `f64` (a float `sum`, or ANY `avg` — it divides at snapshot out of a float running total), and the driver's NEGATIVE fold is exactly the `(S+x)-x != S` arithmetic that is Victor's OPEN decision D4 — the same `retract_ok` derivation `incr_retract_eligible` reads, asked of a rel-backed query for the first time"; }
    if r == DR_MINMAX() { return "an aggregate is `min`/`max` — it retracts by RESCAN over a per-(group, aggregate) value→multiplicity MAP, and that map is a handle field built only on the RETRACTION surface (`want_map = retr && is_mm`), which a rel-backed query does not have; the −1 fold would have nothing to rescan. A MISSING STATE refusal, not an arithmetic one"; }
    return "";
}
pub fn dr_name(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == DR_EMIT()   { return "emit"; }
    if r == DR_FLOAT()  { return "float_acc"; }
    if r == DR_MINMAX() { return "min_max"; }
    return "unset";
}

// ══ THE AGGREGATE'S GROUP-FRAME CLASS (E3) ════════════════════════════════════
pub fn AC_PURE() -> i32 { return 1i32; }   // clauses above the group read key + outputs only
pub fn AC_REP() -> i32  { return 2i32; }   // a clause reads a source row: carry a representative
pub fn ac_render(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == AC_PURE() { return "`select`/`having`/`order by` are over `key` + aggregate outputs only — the group frame is the whole answer"; }
    if r == AC_REP()  { return "a clause above the group names a SOURCE ROW — the group must carry a representative base row"; }
    return "";
}
pub fn ac_verdict(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == AC_PURE() { return "PURE"; }
    if r == AC_REP()  { return "REP"; }
    return "UNSET";
}


// ══ DEMAND FOR A USER REL — magic sets, applied or not, and why (#349) ═══════
// The entry reads rel R with a column bound to a constant or a scalar
// parameter; the rewrite restricts R to that demand (Soufflé's MST, adornment
// one bound column). Each rule names the ONE antecedent that decided it.
pub fn MS_DEMAND() -> i32       { return 1i32; }   // adorned: the rel is evaluated on demand
// 4 (nonlinear), 5 (moves_col), 6 (sel_shape) and 9 (moving_off) are DELETED
// (2026-10-05): the shape-by-shape rewrite they refused in is replaced by the
// magic-sets transformation (`crewrite::core_magic`), which adorns every bound
// occurrence whatever the body's shape. 2 (shared) is kept and now computed
// over that transformation's own graph.
// 7 (cap — no free join-step slot for the magic join) is DELETED with the
// chain's eight-step cap (2026-10-05).
pub fn MS_SHARED() -> i32       { return 2i32; }   // an evaluated clause reads all of R anyway
pub fn MS_NEG_AGG() -> i32      { return 3i32; }   // a body of R aggregates or finds
pub fn MS_FALLIBLE() -> i32     { return 8i32; }   // checked arithmetic could fail outside the demand
pub fn MS_NONREC() -> i32       { return 10i32; }  // not recursive: a restriction saves no evaluation

pub fn ms_render(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == MS_DEMAND()    { return "a reader binds columns of this rel, so only rows carrying the bound values can reach that reader: the reader reads an ADORNED COPY evaluated on demand — its bodies restricted to the values in `__m_<copy>`, which holds one magic rule per bound occurrence (the reader's atoms to the left of it, in max-bound order, and the reader's own magic rel), so the restriction carries into a fixpoint by induction (the magic-sets transformation, Soufflé's MST); a reader that binds nothing still reads the whole rel"; }
    if r == MS_SHARED()    { return "a clause that is evaluated reads the whole rel (it binds none of its columns: the entry, a rel read whole, or an adorned body), so the rel is evaluated whole anyway, and an adorned copy for its bound readers would only add work"; }
    if r == MS_NEG_AGG()   { return "a body of the rel aggregates or finds: such a rel is read whole (Soufflé leaves aggregated relations un-adorned too); an anti join's atom is always read whole and a magic rule never contains one, which only widens a demand"; }
    if r == MS_NONREC()    { return "the rel is not recursive: its body is evaluated whole before a magic join could filter it, so an adorned copy saves no evaluation (the reader's own filter already applies) and would only duplicate its code; demand bounds a FIXPOINT, so only a recursive rel is adorned" ; }
    if r == MS_FALLIBLE()  { return "a body of the rel, or the entry's WHERE / ON, evaluates checked arithmetic (`+ - * / %`, negation), which returns an `ElError` on overflow or division by zero: the naive program evaluates it on rows outside the demand, so restricting the rows could turn an `Err` into an `Ok`. Soufflé's MST excludes order-dependent functors (`/`, `%`) for the same reason; here every integer operator is checked, so all of them count"; }
    return "";
}
pub fn ms_name(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == MS_DEMAND()    { return "demand"; }
    if r == MS_SHARED()    { return "shared"; }
    if r == MS_NEG_AGG()   { return "neg_agg"; }
    if r == MS_FALLIBLE()  { return "fallible"; }
    if r == MS_NONREC()    { return "nonrec"; }
    return "unset";
}
pub fn ms_verdict(r: i32) -> str {
    if r == MS_DEMAND() { return "demand-driven"; }
    return "fully materialized";
}
